+ * Exynos 9820 "downstream parity" knob, default off:
+ * /sys/module/acpm_protocol/parameters/mbox_fixup (the driver is built in).
+ *
+ * mbox_fixup:	mask the APM->AP mailbox interrupts of the polled channels
+ *		(INTMR1) and clear their pending bits (INTCR1) after the RX queue
+ *		was drained, as the Samsung kernel does (acpm_ipc.c channel_init(),
+ *		check_response()). Mainline never touches INTMR1/INTCR1, so the
+ *		APM2AP interrupt (also a PMU wakeup source) stays asserted.
+ *
+ * On the first ACPM_DBG_MAX_DUMPS timeouts every channel's queue pointers,
+ * the init data words and the firmware log are printed.
